Advanced Reconnaissance & OSINT Notes (CEH‑Level)
🔍 1. Google Advanced Search Operators (Google Dorks)
These operators allow precise filtering of Google’s index. They are essential for passive reconnaissance.

Core Operators
site: — Restrict results to a domain
Example: site:eccouncil.org

intitle: — Term must appear in page title
Example: intitle:login site:eccouncil.org

allintitle: — All terms must appear in title
Example: allintitle: detect malware

inurl: — Term must appear in URL
Example: inurl:admin site:target.com

allinurl: — All terms must appear in URL
Example: allinurl: EC-Council career

filetype: — Search specific file formats
Example: EC-Council filetype:pdf ceh

inanchor: — Term must appear in anchor text
Example: Anti-virus inanchor:Norton

allinanchor: — All terms must appear in anchor text
Example: allinanchor: best cloud service provider

info: — Google’s info page about a domain
Example: info:eccouncil.org

